Package: killerPals
Title: Colourblind-Friendly Colour Palettes Inspired by Queen Album Covers
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Noah", "Weidig", email = "weidignc@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Forty-eight colour palettes derived from the fifteen Queen studio
    album covers, with qualitative, sequential and diverging variants for every
    album. Palettes are optimised so that their worst-case pairwise CIEDE2000
    separation stays high under simulated deuteranopic, protanopic and
    tritanopic vision, and so that every colour clears a minimum contrast ratio
    against light and dark backgrounds. Sequential and diverging palettes are
    strictly monotone in lightness, so they survive greyscale printing.
    Includes 'ggplot2' scales for discrete, continuous and binned aesthetics,
    plus tools to simulate colour vision deficiency and audit any palette's
    accessibility.
